---Assignment Questions
---ROWID
---1. Retrieve the ROWID for all rows in the Countries table.
select ROWID from Countries;

---2. Find the ROWID for the row where the Country_Name is 'India'.
select ROWID from Countries WHERE Country_Name ='India';

---3. Delete a row from the Cities table using its ROWID.
DELETE FROM Cities WHERE ROWID = 'AALxHjAABAAMsHPAAA';

---4. Retrieve all distinct ROWID values for the States table.
SELECT DISTINCT ROWID FROM States;

---5. Identify rows in the Cities table with the same ROWID.
SELECT ROWID, COUNT(*)
FROM Cities
GROUP BY ROWID
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

